# Third-Party Licenses

This project is a clean-room implementation and contains no code from
Excalidraw or tldraw. The following permissively-licensed libraries are used at
runtime; their license texts ship with the packages in node_modules and are
reproduced in distribution bundles as required.

| Library | License | Purpose | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| roughjs | MIT | Hand-drawn/sketchy shape rendering | in use |
| perfect-freehand | MIT | Pressure-sensitive freehand ink strokes | in use |
| fractional-indexing | CC0 | Stable ordering keys for element z-index | in use |

## Desktop app (Rust crates)

Linked into the Tauri shell (`apps/desktop/src-tauri`). Everything below the Tauri
framework itself is for the LAN relay, which lets the desktop app host a
collaboration room on a local network with no internet.

| Crate | License | Purpose | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| tauri (+ official plugins) | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | Desktop shell, windowing, updater, dialogs | in use |
| serde / serde_json | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | Command payloads; relay frame parsing | in use |
| base64 | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | Encoding for file bridge and role tokens | in use |
| tokio | MIT | Async runtime for the LAN relay | in use |
| tokio-tungstenite | MIT | WebSocket transport for the LAN relay | in use |
| futures-util | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | Stream/sink adapters over the relay socket | in use |
| hmac / sha2 | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | HMAC-SHA256 room role tokens (`lan_relay/tokens.rs`) | in use |
| uuid | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | Room ids, peer ids, per-session token secret | in use |
| if-addrs | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | Enumerating this machine's private addresses | in use |

Update this file whenever a runtime dependency is added or removed.
